# Line endings.
#
# Shell scripts must stay LF even when checked out on Windows. docker/start.sh
# is the container's entrypoint, and bash reading a CRLF script fails on the
# shebang with "bad interpreter" — a confusing way to discover a line-ending
# problem. Dockerfiles are pinned for the same reason.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Git LFS is deliberately NOT configured here. The 13 files over 10 MB (the
# OSM street layers, up to 29 MB) are already in history as plain blobs, and
# GitHub has no size problem with them. Only Hugging Face does — so LFS is set
# up in the Space repo instead, by deploy/hf-space/assemble.sh, which writes
# its own .gitattributes before staging anything. Adding LFS patterns here
# would route new data files into GitHub's 1 GB LFS quota for no benefit.
